# @DISK
# S5_disk (D-SESSIONS, 2026-11-06): a program kept on disk the way users did --
# SAVE (tokenised and ,A), FILES, NEW + LOAD, MERGE of an ASCII file over a typed
# program, NAME, KILL, LOAD ,R and RUN "file", and the errors a typo gives
# (a missing file, MERGE of a tokenised file). CF-3300 + the DISK target.
NEW
10 PRINT "MAIN PROGRAM"
20 GOSUB 100
30 END
100 PRINT "OLD SUB":RETURN
SAVE "MAIN"
SAVE "MAINA",A
FILES
NEW
100 PRINT "NEW SUB":RETURN
110 RETURN
SAVE "SUBS",A
NEW
LOAD "MAIN"
LIST
MERGE "SUBS"
LIST
RUN
MERGE "MAIN"
LIST
NAME "SUBS" AS "PARTS"
FILES
LOAD "SUBS"
KILL "MAINA"
FILES
LOAD "MAIN",R
RUN "PARTS"
LIST
PRINT "DONE"
